WEBVTT

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.240
Hi, I'm Tom Smothers.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.820
And I'm Dick Smothers, and welcome to the original Smothers Brothers Comedy Hour.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.180
These shows were taped to Television City in Hollywood during the late 60s.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:16.210
This Comedy Hour, you're about to see, was scheduled to air April 13th, 1969.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.930
But if you don't remember seeing it before, it may be because CBS never, ever aired this show.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.950
That's right, and our guests on the show that was never aired were Laugh-In's Dan Rowan,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.690
comedian David Steinberg, and singer Nancy Wilson.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:29.970
This Comedy Hour...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.040
actually is one of my most memorable shows.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.960
And that's because this is the comedy hour that supposedly got us fired.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:36.520
That's right.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.360
This was the second time David Steinberg performed a satyrical religious sermon on the show.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.480
The first time David performed one of his sermons on the show, CBS got hundreds of negative letters, actually.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.640
So they were wary of having him back on the show again, and of course we had him on the show

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.810
and asked him to do another second sermon.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.030
Because it went over so well with the network.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.970
So the second sermon they used as a...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.800
excuse to fire the Smothers Brothers. One of our other guests was Dan Rowan from the

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:09.030
NBC series Laugh-In and he also knew about censorship firsthand. Our musical guest was

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:13.950
the great jazz singer Nancy Wilson. I had the honor of singing a duet with her which was outstanding,

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:19.100
I might say myself. So let's have a first look at the Smothers Brothers Comedy Hour

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.220
that was never aired on CBS. Never.

